The repository appears to be empty on GitHub. That said, based on the error log and the index.py you shared, here are the most likely causes and fixes:

What's likely going wrong
1. Missing or incomplete requirements.txt
This is the #1 cause of FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED on Vercel. Your index.py imports mangum and main, so at minimum you need:

fastapi
mangum
Plus any other packages your main.py uses (SQLAlchemy, psycopg2, etc.). If this file is missing or incomplete, Vercel silently fails to install deps and the function crashes on import.

2. Wrong vercel.json configuration
Vercel needs to know to route all requests through your Python function. You need a vercel.json like this:

json
{
  "rewrites": [
    { "source": "/(.*)", "destination": "/api/index.py" }
  ]
}
Without this, /favicon.ico and other routes won't hit your handler correctly.

3. main.py must be inside the api/ folder (or use the right import path)
Vercel runs each file in api/ in isolation. If main.py is at the project root and index.py is in api/, the import from main import app will fail because the root isn't on the Python path.

Fix: Either move main.py into api/, or restructure like this:

api/
  index.py
  main.py         ← move it here
  requirements.txt  ← or at root
4. /favicon.ico triggering a 500
The fact that even a favicon request causes a 500 means the function is crashing on startup (import errors), not on a specific route. This points back to issue #1 or #3 above.

Quick checklist
Check
☐	requirements.txt exists and includes fastapi, mangum, and all other deps
☐	main.py is in the same directory as index.py (both in api/)
☐	vercel.json has a rewrite rule pointing to /api/index.py
☐	No env variables are missing (database URLs, secret keys, etc.)
