10:45 AM
Now the problem is very clear. There are multiple issues causing the crash:

Issue 1: Circular import — api/index.py imports main, which imports from api import ...
Your file structure is:

api/
  index.py     ← Vercel entry point
  auth.py
  bills.py
  ...
main.py        ← imports "from api import auth, bills..."
When index.py does from main import app, and main.py does from api import auth, Python gets confused because api is both a package (the folder) and the place index.py lives. This causes an ImportError or ModuleNotFoundError on startup.

Issue 2: StaticFiles mount will crash on Vercel
python
app.mount("/", StaticFiles(directory="static", html=True), name="static")
Vercel serverless functions don't have a persistent filesystem. The static/ directory won't exist, so this line throws an error at startup — before any request is even handled.

Issue 3: create_tables() on every cold start
Calling await create_tables() on every startup is risky on serverless — if the DB connection fails or times out, the whole function crashes.

The Fix
Step 1 — Restructure your project
Move everything out of the api/ folder conflict. Rename your routers folder:

api/
  index.py          ← Vercel entry (keep as-is)
routers/            ← rename from "api" to "routers"
  auth.py
  projects.py
  bills.py
  ... etc
main.py
database.py
static/
Step 2 — Update main.py imports
python
from routers import (
    auth,
    projects,
    bills,
    labour,
    uploads,
    materials,
    payments,
    contracts,
    notifications,
    ocr,
    reports,
    ai,
    daily_logs,
)
Step 3 — Remove the StaticFiles mount
Vercel serves your frontend as static files separately. Remove this line from main.py:

python
# DELETE this line:
app.mount("/", StaticFiles(directory="static", html=True), name="static")
Serve your frontend via Vercel's static output instead — put your HTML/CSS/JS in a public/ folder and add to vercel.json:

json
{
  "outputDirectory": "public",
  "rewrites": [
    { "source": "/api/(.*)", "destination": "/api/index.py" }
  ]
}
Step 4 — Guard create_tables() from crashing the app
python
@app.on_event("startup")
async def startup():
    try:
        await create_tables()
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"DB init warning: {e}")  # log but don't crash
Step 5 — Verify requirements.txt at project root
Make sure it includes everything:

fastapi
mangum
sqlalchemy
asyncpg        # or psycopg2, depending on your DB
python-multipart
pillow         # if OCR/uploads use it
python-jose    # if auth uses JWT
passlib
httpx
Summary of changes
Problem	Fix
🔴	api/ folder name conflicts with Vercel entry point	Rename routers folder to routers/
🔴	StaticFiles crashes on serverless (no filesystem)	Remove it; serve frontend via public/
🟡	DB startup crash kills the whole function	Wrap in try/except
🟡	Missing deps in requirements.txt	Add all packages
The rename of api/ → routers/ and removing StaticFiles are the two critical fixes that will get you unblocked immediately.

